fuxi: 0135 -- the shell also answers on the frame channel

0134 put the debug shell on the UDP command socket, and on hardware that socket
turns out not to answer: "stat" over UDP gets no reply while the same command
over an 0x88B5 frame does.  The frame path (0106) is the one that was proven on
the phone -- it needs no kernel socket, no IP stack, and no interface address,
which is exactly the situation a wedged boot leaves you in.

So the dispatcher the frame path already uses (ud_cmd) now calls the shell first
and sends its reply as frames, one per ETHER_MAX_LEN-sized chunk, ending with the
same "[[fuxi-shell-end]]" marker.  Verbs that need this driver's own state (fb,
stat, cpu) stay where they were.

tools/fuxi-ethcmd.py reads the reply until that marker, so it is now the client
for a shell that works on a boot where UDP does not:

  sudo tools/fuxi-ethcmd.py enx02005e77ee01 ps 20

Harness: applied=134 skipped=0.  Why the UDP socket stops answering is still
open; it is not this patch's problem, and the frame path is enough to debug with.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/fuxi_usb.c b/bsd/dev/fuxi_usb.c
index 6500e3b..e507636 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/fuxi_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/fuxi_usb.c
@@ -584,6 +584,33 @@ ud_cmd(const char *line)
 		fuxi_soc_reset();
 		return;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * The debug shell (patch 0134) speaks the same vocabulary on both paths.
+	 * It goes first, so "help" here lists what 0135 added; the verbs below
+	 * stay for the ones that need this driver's own state (fb, stat, cpu).
+	 */
+	{
+		extern int fuxi_shell_command(const char *line);
+		extern void fuxi_shell_end(void);
+		extern const char *fuxi_shell_out(size_t *len);
+		const char *out;
+		size_t out_len = 0;
+		size_t off = 0;
+
+		if (fuxi_shell_command(line)) {
+			fuxi_shell_end();
+			out = fuxi_shell_out(&out_len);
+			while (off < out_len) {
+				size_t chunk = out_len - off;
+				if (chunk > FUXI_CMD_FRAME_MAX) {
+					chunk = FUXI_CMD_FRAME_MAX;
+				}
+				ud_cmd_send(out + off, chunk);
+				off += chunk;
+			}
+			return;
+		}
+	}
 	if (len == 4 && strncmp(line, "help", 4) == 0) {
 		n = snprintf(reply, sizeof(reply),
 		    "fuxi: stat | cpu | fb [scale] | echo <text> | restart | help\n");
